<br/>
<h3 id="how_big_are_the_upgrades">How Big Are the Upgrades?</h3><br/>
Apple's own comparisons against the outgoing chips are heavily weighted toward AI and graphics. For the M5 Max against the M4 Max, Apple claims:<br/>
<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li>Up to <strong>3.9x faster</strong> LLM prompt processing in LM Studio</li><br/>
<li>Up to <strong>3.5x faster</strong> text-to-image performance</li><br/>
<li>Up to <strong>3x faster</strong> Magic Mask performance in Blackmagic Design DaVinci Resolve Studio</li><br/>
<li>Up to <strong>1.9x faster</strong> basecalling for DNA sequencing in Oxford Nanopore MinKNOW</li><br/>
<li>Up to <strong>50%</strong> faster graphics performance</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<br/>
For the M5 Ultra against the M3 Ultra, Apple claims:<br/>
<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li>Up to <strong>4.3x faster</strong> text-to-image performance</li><br/>
<li>Up to <strong>4x faster</strong> LLM prompt processing in LM Studio</li><br/>
<li>Up to <strong>3.3x faster</strong> CopyCat ML training performance in Foundry Nuke</li><br/>
<li>Up to <strong>1.8x faster</strong> graphics performance</li><br/>
<li>Up to <strong>1.7x faster</strong> scene rendering performance in Maxon Redshift</li><br/>
<li>Up to <strong>1.3x higher</strong> multithreaded CPU performance</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
<br/>
On either chip, tasks that use matrix multiplication can run three to four times faster thanks to new Neural Accelerators in each GPU core.<br/>
<br/>
<h2 id="which_to_choose">Which to Choose?</h2><br/>
Apple no longer sells the M4 Max or M3 Ultra models, which became relatively poor value for money by the end of their run. The M4 Max cost &#36;2,499 with a 14-core CPU and up to 64GB of memory. For the same price, the M5 Max has an 18-core CPU, 614GB/s memory bandwidth, up to 128GB of memory, twice-fast storage, and Wi‑Fi 7. The M3 Ultra ended at &#36;5,299 with a 96GB memory limit. For &#36;200 more, the M5 Ultra brings back 256GB and 512GB options and adds 50% more memory bandwidth.<br/>
<br/>
Current M4 Max and M3 Ultra owners generally do not need to upgrade after only 17 months. Launch buyers paid &#36;1,999 or &#36;3,999, so replacing their machine now costs 25–38% more for the same design, ports, Ultra core limits, storage limit, and Media Engine. The main exception is AI-heavy work. Local LLMs, on-device image or video generation, and demanding machine-learning tasks in applications like DaVinci Resolve or Nuke can benefit substantially from the new Neural Accelerators. The M5 Ultra's 1.2TB/s memory bandwidth can also improve large-model token generation.<br/>
<br/>
The upgrade makes more sense for <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/m1/">M1</a> or <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/m2/">M2</a> &zwnj;Mac Studio&zwnj; owners. Apple says the M5 Max can process prompts up to 10.7× faster than the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/m1-max/">M1 Max</a>, while the M5 Ultra can train ML models up to 15.4× faster than the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/m1-ultra/">M1 Ultra</a>. Older models also lack Thunderbolt 5, AV1 decoding, and the newer Media Engine. If you already skipped the 2025 refresh, this is a more meaningful step forward.<br/>
<br/>
The 2025 models are mainly worth considering used or refurbished at a steep discount. Apple raised prices in June, so lightly discounted older stock is often too close in price to a new model. One notable exception is an M3 Ultra with 256GB or 512GB of memory, since those configurations were unavailable new for much of 2026 and M5 Ultra equivalents will not ship until later this year.<br/>
<br/>
When configuring, buyers should remember that memory and graphics are linked. The M5 Max always has an 18-core CPU, so the key choices are GPU and memory. More than 36GB of memory requires the 40-core GPU. With the M5 Ultra, 512GB of memory requires the 80-core GPU. If memory is your limit, as it often is for local AI tasks, you may need to pay for more GPU cores too. Apple says the 512GB M5 Ultra arrives in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/mac-studio-m5-ultra-512gb-ram-october/">late October</a>, with pricing expected to start above &#36;10,000.<br/>
<br/>
The M5 Ultra is now Apple's highest-end Mac. Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/26/apple-discontinues-mac-pro/">discontinued the Mac Pro</a> in March, seemingly with no plans for a replacement. There is no higher end Mac to wait for and no internal expansion path beyond adding a second machine.<br/>
